# Local environment files (never commit secrets). .env.example stays tracked as a template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .env.production holds ONLY public client values (Supabase URL + publishable
# anon key) that Vite must inline into the browser bundle at build time. These
# are not secrets — they ship to every visitor's browser and are protected by
# Row-Level Security, not by being hidden. Tracked so production builds (e.g.
# Cloudflare) always have them regardless of dashboard env-var config.
!.env.production
supabase/.temp/
